<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_0074e29f31a1f0feb082e0064bee46f60bf6b5ae3f8703d1231341374ed97e52_n0007/tu_0011> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Target BP is 130/80 mmHg Hypertension is linked to immunosuppressive therapy and denervation of cardiac volume receptors It is sensitive to a low-sodium diet. Treatment with amlodipine and ACEIs/ARBs are first choice, usually completed by diuretics. Beta-blockers are contra-indicated as they hamper the already delayed chronotropic response of the denervated heart during the early term but they showed the beneficial effects as a treatment more than 1–1.5 years after HTX and in the case of post-transplant heart failure development. Nifedipine and diltiazem may increase the effects of calcineurin inhibitors due to the drug interactions" .
