<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_0074e29f31a1f0feb082e0064bee46f60bf6b5ae3f8703d1231341374ed97e52_n0007/tu_0005> <http://digistrucmed.org/verbatimText> "level, slowly progressing warm-up, closed-chain resistive activities (e.g. bridging, half-squats, toe raises, use of therapeutic bands) and walking/Nordic walking/cycling Resistance training: 2–3 sets with 10–12 repetitions per set at 40–70% 1-RM, with a full recovery period >1 min between each set. The goal is to be able to do five sets of 10 repetitions at 70% of 1-RM Aerobic training should start at low intensity ( VO_{2peak} < 50\\% or 10% below anaerobic threshold) or peak work load (<50%) and progressively increase HIIT: sets of short- or long-lasting exertion periods (30 s to 4 min) at high intensity (> 85% VO_{2max} ), followed by short- or long-lasting recovery periods (30 s to 4 min). 79" .
